      <p class="eyebrow">Founder &amp; Principal Engineer</p>
      <h2 id="founder-title">Jeremy Shows</h2>
      <p>Before working on distributed systems and AI software, Jeremy worked as a mechanic, race-car builder, fabricator, IT professional, and small-business owner. That experience shapes a practical engineering lens: understand the parts, their connections, and what happens when one fails.</p>
      <p>ForgeWire Labs focuses on systems that remain understandable under changing requirements, limited hardware, and operator intervention. Projects are kept independent so each can stand on its own and carry its own maturity boundary.</p>
      <a class="text-link" href="https://github.com/ForgeWireLabs">Explore the public repositories <span aria-hidden="true">↗</span></a>
    </div>
  </div>
</section>

<section class="about-statement">
  <div class="page-shell">
    <p class="statement-quote">Build it. Test it under failure. Preserve the evidence. Understand its limits. Then decide whether it is useful.</p>
    <p class="statement-credit">A working principle from ForgeWire Labs</p>
  </div>
</section>

